Now, each candy costs 6 tickets. To find out how many candies he can buy, we need to divide the total tickets by the cost per candy. So, 42 divided by 6. Let me do that division. 6 times 7 is 42, right? 6*7=42. So that means he can buy 7 candies.

Wait, but let me check if there's any detail I might have missed. The problem says he was trying to buy candy that costs 6 tickets a piece. So, no, there's no mention of any discounts or anything. It's straightforward. So, 42 divided by 6 is exactly 7. So, he can buy 7 candies. That seems right.

