Next, the store places these bears onto shelves, with 9 bears on each shelf. To find out how many shelves are needed, I need to divide the total number of bears by the number of bears per shelf. 

So, 27 divided by 9. Since 9 multiplied by 3 equals 27, the division comes out even. This means exactly 3 shelves are required. 

