The problem involves determining the number of students in each group after some are excluded. By subtracting those not picked from the total, we find the number of students assigned to groups, then dividing by the number of groups gives the answer. 

$$
\text{Total students} = 65 \\
\text{Students not picked} = 17 \\
\text{Students picked} = 65 - 17 = 48 \\
\text{Number of groups} = 8 \\
\text{Students per group} = \frac{48}{8} = 6
$$

The final answer is \boxed{6}.
