Wait, how do I subtract 17 from 65? Let me think. Maybe I can break it down. 17 is 10 + 7. So if I take away 10 from 65, that would be 55, and then take away 7 more. 55 - 7 is 48. So, 48 students were picked. 

Now, the problem says the rest were put into 8 groups. So, those 48 students are divided into 8 groups. I need to find out how many students are in each group. That means I need to divide 48 by 8. 

