Will initially had 59 pieces of clothing to wash. He washed 32 of them in one load, so the number of clothing items left to be washed is calculated as:

$$
59 - 32 = 27
$$

He then decides to split these 27 pieces of clothing into 9 equal loads. To find out how many pieces go into each load, we divide:

$$
27 \div 9 = 3
$$

Thus, the number of pieces of clothing that can go in each of the small loads is:

$$
\boxed{3}
$$

