Janet bought a total of 6 country albums and 2 pop albums. Each album contains 9 songs. To find the total number of songs, we first calculate the total number of albums:

$$
6 \text{ (country albums)} + 2 \text{ (pop albums)} = 8 \text{ albums}
$$

Each album has 9 songs, so the total number of songs is:

$$
8 \text{ albums} \times 9 \text{ songs per album} = 72 \text{ songs}
$$

We can also verify this by calculating the number of songs from each genre separately:

$$
6 \text{ (country albums)} \times 9 \text{ songs per album} = 54 \text{ songs}
$$
$$
2 \text{ (pop albums)} \times 9 \text{ songs per album} = 18 \text{ songs}
$$

Adding these together gives:

$$
54 \text{ songs} + 18 \text{ songs} = 72 \text{ songs}
$$

Thus, the total number of songs Janet bought is $\boxed{72}$.  
